title: Receipt ingestion: upload to ledger
description: How a receipt photo travels across 6 systems before it lands as a booked transaction.
direction: right

user: Bookkeeper [person]
mobile: Mobile app [rounded, detail: iOS / Android]

group edge: Edge [gray] {
  cdn: CloudFront [cloud]
  gw: API gateway [hexagon, detail: auth · rate limit]
}
group ingest: Ingestion [blue] {
  upload: Upload service [detail: Go]
  s3: Raw images [cylinder, detail: S3]
  q1: ingest.received [pill]
}
group ml: Extraction [purple] {
  ocr: OCR worker [detail: GPU pool]
  extract: Field extractor [detail: LLM]
  conf: Confidence ≥ 0.9? [diamond]
}
group review: Human review [orange] {
  hq: Review queue [pill]
  ops: Ops reviewer [person]
}
group ledger: Accounting [green] {
  match: Bank matcher
  pub: Publisher [detail: Xero / QBO]
  db: Ledger DB [cylinder, detail: Postgres]
}
xero: Xero / QuickBooks [cloud]

user -> mobile: snaps photo
mobile -> cdn -> gw
gw -> upload: PUT /receipts
upload -> s3: store
upload ..> q1: event
q1 ..> ocr
ocr -> extract: text blocks
extract -> conf
conf -> match: yes
conf -> hq: no
hq ..> ops
ops -> match: corrected
match -> db
match -> pub
pub => xero: publish [red]

comment on conf by deyan: Where does the 0.9 threshold come from? Per-client?
comment on pub->xero by ana: Retries? Xero rate limits at 60/min.
